# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/herbalism
title Herbalism 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Ironforge

# Herbalism 1-300 for both factions: loops through the densest skill-up herbs
# for each skill band (expected skill-ups per yard walked), with rank training.
# A zone counts the herbs it keeps up at once (the Forever server's spawn pools,
# tools/lib/professions/gathering/node-abundance.json), not every spot a herb can use.
# Skill needed per herb: Peacebloom, Silverleaf 1, Earthroot 15, Mageroyal 50,
# Briarthorn 70, Stranglekelp 85, Bruiseweed 100, Wild Steelbloom 115, Grave
# Moss 120, Kingsblood 125, Liferoot 150, Fadeleaf 160, Goldthorn 170,
# Khadgar's Whisker 185, Wintersbite 195, Firebloom 205, Purple Lotus 210,
# Arthas' Tears 220, Sungrass 230, Blindweed 235, Ghost Mushroom 245,
# Gromsblood 250, Golden Sansam 260, Dreamfoil 270, Mountain Silversage 280,
# Plaguebloom 285, Icecap 290, Black Lotus 300.
#
# Spawns come from the reference data: the Era baseline (pfQuest) plus the
# node spawns Forever's beta sniffs add (Zephras Isle, the starting-area Poor
# Copper Veins and herbs: the Forever TrinityCore world DB); trainer learn skills
# and prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists; recipes and their skill colours
# from the Forever client tables (`forge data professions`).
# ASSUMED: past level 30 (the beta's cap) Forever's spawns are Classic's; nothing
# confirms them yet. In-game check: refine with Polestar_Recorder sessions.
# Ranks ask no character level: Forever's sniffed trainer lists carry none for
# Herbalism, Mining or Skinning, and level 10 for Journeyman crafting and Fishing.
# INGAME: does a gathering trainer ask a level for Expert or Artisan? (our data:
# none; one web guide: Expert 10, Artisan 25).
# Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine converts them where Forever
# changed a map frame, and a map without an Era frame (Zephras Isle) compiles live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice
section Herbalism 1-50

step Learn Herbalism
  tip Any Herbalism trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Herbalism at any level (10c), and so does the Junior Herbalism Trainer in each starting area; the arrow picks the nearest. Turn on Find Herbs (spellbook, General tab) so herbs show on the minimap. Forever's starting areas also have Wilted Peacebloom and Stunted Silverleaf (skill 1). The first-hour quest of each starting area (Rascally Rodents, Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery, The Woodland Protector, Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise, A Humble Task, Marla's Last Wish) offers Wild Harvest as a reward: reading it gives 2 skill, up to 15. Trade goods vendors sell the Apprentice's Herb Pouch, a four-slot bag for herbs (25c). If you sat at your starting area's campfire for The Great Outdoors, the camping guide there also offers Camping 101: Herbalism: hand it in to the herbalism trainer it names once you reach skill 20, for the Incense Candle recipe.
  train Herbalism Apprentice

